diff --git a/apps/zcode-cli/docs/provider-subscriptions.md b/apps/zcode-cli/docs/provider-subscriptions.md
index f213185..c3d0635 100644
--- a/apps/zcode-cli/docs/provider-subscriptions.md
+++ b/apps/zcode-cli/docs/provider-subscriptions.md
@@ -596,3 +596,67 @@ expiry or paid billing period. Keep unknown future tier names rather than mappin
 Reuse the existing account badge and original plan-status card; known tiers receive established
 semantic color tokens. Original ProviderDetailFeedback and SectionLayout remain byte-identical to
 the pin; only failure copy/classification/manual dismissal differs from upstream.
+
+### Source-backed protocol and minimal credential controls
+
+Each preset service/region/auth route exposes only explicitly declared wire formats. A custom
+address can offer adapter formats as user choices, but none is a claim the upstream host supports
+it. Imported routes retain their source protocol and never borrow another vendor's endpoint.
+The official provider documents, source-client transformation, and candidate adapter must agree
+before adding a preset route. Unsupported/unknown formats remain absent from that preset. A model
+catalog GET is not proof of Responses streaming/tool semantics. Claude subscription is distinct
+from Anthropic API and CC Switch's Claude API-key row; no native Claude account login/runtime is
+registered until the unmodified official client path and Fleet Session/permission/usage bridges are
+implemented and verified.
+
+The existing ProviderSettings owner still commits one credential row at a time. For a saved or new
+API key, Enter or input blur commits only that row; Escape restores its saved value. A blank new
+row stays local. Clearing the only saved key removes it on blur without a trash icon. A second
+visible row reveals removal; a second saved identity reveals per-key enable/default controls and
+the automatic-switch section. A single subscription account hides the trash/switch controls but
+retains an explicit disconnect action in its opened account details. None of these actions writes
+other pending address/name/model drafts. Late Host responses cannot overwrite newer edits.
+
+Preset format changes on a saved connection additionally require identical built-in model IDs.
+OpenCode Go/Zen publish model-specific Chat, Messages and Responses endpoints; choosing a
+different format while creating a connection selects the matching sibling template and its model
+list. A saved connection cannot swap its protocol while keeping models from another route.
+Alibaba Coding Plan explicitly excludes Responses; its Chat and Messages endpoints and keys
+are plan/region-specific. DeepSeek and xAI do document Responses, but catalog GET alone never
+certifies streaming/tool semantics. Custom addresses remain user-declared protocol choices.
+
+Acceptance from an isolated desktop profile: the one saved synthetic key showed no confirm,
+trash, per-key toggle or automatic switch; changing it and blurring saved through ProviderSettings.
+A second unsaved row showed removal but no automatic switch; blurring a distinct second synthetic
+key saved it and enabled the controls. Removing that key collapsed back to the single-row layout.
+Clearing the final key on blur removed its persisted value and disabled discovery. No real key or
+provider request was used. The current Claude subscription lane is still absent, not an API alias.
+
+### Preset route audit
+
+This is the 19-vendor/41-template registry projection, not a list of verified paid accounts.
+“Chat” means OpenAI Chat Completions, “Messages” Anthropic Messages, and “Responses”
+OpenAI Responses. A dash means no registered route, not that the company sells no such plan.
+Every route still needs that account's model catalog and a real request before it is called ready.
+
+| Vendor/product | API preset | Subscription or plan-key preset | Boundary checked |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Z.ai / BigModel | Chat | Coding Plan Messages | Coding key and general API endpoint are separate ([ZCode source](https://zcode.z.ai/en/docs/configuration)). |
+| Kimi / Moonshot | Messages | Kimi Code Messages | Kimi Code also documents Chat, but no Responses ([model guide](https://www.kimi.com/code/docs/en/kimi-code/models.html)). |
+| MiniMax | Messages | Token Plan Messages | Plan key and paid API balance differ ([Token Plan](https://platform.minimax.io/subscribe/token-plan)). |
+| DeepSeek | Chat, Messages | — | Responses is documented separately; current preset remains the two tested routes ([official guide](https://api-docs.deepseek.com/guides/responses_api/)). |
+| Alibaba Model Studio | Chat, Messages, by region | Coding Plan and Token Plan Chat | Plan-specific keys and endpoints; Coding Plan explicitly excludes Responses ([FAQ](https://help.aliyun.com/en/model-studio/coding-plan-faq)). |
+| Xiaomi MiMo | Messages | Token Plan Chat | Model/format coverage varies; no inferred Responses plan route ([MiMo docs](https://platform.xiaomimimo.com/docs/en-US/usage-guide/passing-back-reasoning_content)). |
+| OpenAI | Responses | ChatGPT native account | API balance and ChatGPT subscription use different credentials. |
+| Anthropic | Messages | — | Claude subscription needs the unmodified native Claude Code executor ([policy](https://code.claude.com/docs/en/legal-and-compliance)). |
+| xAI | Responses | Grok native account | API key and Grok account differ ([API reference](https://docs.x.ai/developers/rest-api-reference/inference/responses)). |
+| OpenRouter | Messages | — | Gateway route is user account dependent ([Messages reference](https://openrouter.ai/docs/api/api-reference/anthropic-messages/create-messages)). |
+| OpenCode | Zen: mixed per-model routes | Go: mixed per-model routes | Chat/Messages/Responses models are not interchangeable ([Go](https://opencode.ai/docs/go/), [Zen](https://opencode.ai/docs/zen)). |
+| GitHub | — | Copilot native account | Account catalog, not a general GitHub API key. |
+| Groq | Chat | — | Responses exists but is a separate model/endpoint contract ([compatibility](https://console.groq.com/docs/openai)). |
+| Cerebras | Chat | — | [Chat reference](https://inference-docs.cerebras.ai/api-reference/chat-completions). |
+| Mistral | Chat | — | [Chat reference](https://docs.mistral.ai/api). |
+| NVIDIA | Chat | — | [NIM LLM endpoints](https://docs.api.nvidia.com/nim/reference/llm-apis). |
+| Together AI | Chat | — | Current catalog route only; live execution is unverified. |
+| Google | Chat compatibility | — | Native Gemini consumer login is absent ([compatibility](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/openai)). |
+| SiliconFlow | Chat | — | [Chat reference](https://docs.siliconflow.cn/docs/api/chat-completions-post). |
